@namespace MirbadLLM.Web.Components.ModelEditor
@using System.Globalization
@using MirbadLLM.Agent.Contracts
@* The llama.cpp model editor's GGUF picker (design-p3p4 §A.7, MN-226). Two shapes:
   - a Hugging Face GGUF repo (Variants set): one row per quantization with its size, split parts and its fit on each GPU
     of the chosen node. Before the download only the file size is known, so the fit is a lower bound ("needs at least",
     weights × 1.10 + one CUDA context); the vision projectors (mmproj) are listed separately;
   - a folder on the node (Folder set): its model GGUF (picked from the agent's list when it holds several), its header
     summary (through IAgentClient.InspectGgufAsync, the gguf.inspect route) and the estimate's fit on each GPU. *@
<div class="gguf-picker" data-testid="gguf-picker">
    @if (Variants is { } variants)
    {
        <div class="gguf-table-wrap">
            <table class="data-table data-table--stack gguf-variants" data-testid="gguf-variants">
                <caption class="visually-hidden">GGUF variants of the repo, with their fit on each GPU</caption>
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="col" class="col-check"><span class="visually-hidden">Choose</span></th>
                        <th scope="col">Variant</th>
                        <th scope="col">Size</th>
                        <th scope="col">Parts</th>
                        <th scope="col">Fit</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    @foreach (var variant in variants)
                    {
                        string id = "gguf-variant-" + Slug(variant.Name);
                        bool on = string.Equals(variant.Name, SelectedVariant, StringComparison.Ordinal);
                        double need = LlamaCppEditing.MinimumNeedGiB(variant.TotalBytes, CpuOnly);
                        <tr data-testid="@id" class="@(on ? "gguf-row--on" : null)">
                            <td class="col-check">
                                <input type="radio" class="form-check-input" name="gguf-variant" id="@id-radio" data-testid="@($"{id}-radio")"
                                       checked="@on" aria-describedby="@id-fit" @onchange="() => SelectedVariantChanged.InvokeAsync(variant.Name)" />
                            </td>
                            <td class="col-primary"><label for="@id-radio" class="num">@variant.Name</label></td>
                            <td data-label="Size" class="num">@UiFormat.Bytes(variant.TotalBytes)</td>
                            <td data-label="Parts" class="num">@variant.FileCount.ToString(CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)</td>
                            <td data-label="Fit" id="@id-fit" data-testid="@($"{id}-fit")">
                                @FitLines(need, atLeast: true)
                            </td>
                        </tr>
                    }
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <div class="field-hint" data-testid="gguf-variants-hint">
            @if (CpuOnly)
            {
                <span>Before the download only the size is known, so each fit counts the weights alone (× 1.10), all of them in host RAM: this node has no GPU.</span>
            }
            else
            {
                <span>Before the download only the size is known, so each fit counts the weights alone (× 1.10, plus
                <span class="num">@UiFormat.GiB(MirbadLLM.Orchestration.Multinode.LlamaCppMemoryEstimate.CudaContextGiBPerGpu)</span> CUDA context).</span>
            }
            The KV cache and compute buffers are added once the download has read the file's header.
        </div>

        @if (Projectors.Count > 0)
        {
            <fieldset class="gguf-projectors" data-testid="gguf-projectors">
                <legend class="field-label">Vision projector (mmproj)</legend>
                <label class="form-check">
                    <input type="radio" class="form-check-input" name="gguf-projector" data-testid="gguf-projector-none"
                           checked="@string.IsNullOrEmpty(SelectedProjector)" @onchange="() => SelectedProjectorChanged.InvokeAsync(string.Empty)" />
                    <span class="form-check-label">None (text or embedding model)</span>
                </label>
                @foreach (var projector in Projectors)
                {
                    <label class="form-check">
                        <input type="radio" class="form-check-input" name="gguf-projector" data-testid="@($"gguf-projector-{Slug(projector.Name)}")"
                               checked="@string.Equals(projector.Name, SelectedProjector, StringComparison.Ordinal)"
                               @onchange="() => SelectedProjectorChanged.InvokeAsync(projector.Name)" />
                        <span class="form-check-label"><span class="num">@projector.Name</span> · <span class="num">@UiFormat.Bytes(projector.Bytes)</span></span>
                    </label>
                }
            </fieldset>
        }
    }
    else if (Folder is not null)
    {
        <div class="field">
            <FieldHelp Label="GGUF file" For="field-gguf-file" Help="@LlamaCppFieldHelp.GgufFile" />
            <div class="gguf-file-row">
                @if (Candidates.Count > 0)
                {
                    <select class="form-select num" id="field-gguf-file" data-testid="field-gguf-file" value="@File"
                            @onchange="e => OnFileChosenAsync(e.Value as string)">
                        <option value="">Choose a GGUF</option>
                        @foreach (string candidate in Candidates)
                        {
                            <option value="@candidate">@candidate</option>
                        }
                    </select>
                }
                else
                {
                    <input class="form-control num" id="field-gguf-file" data-testid="field-gguf-file" value="@File" placeholder="The folder's only GGUF"
                           autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" @onchange="e => FileChanged.InvokeAsync(e.Value as string ?? string.Empty)" />
                }
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" data-testid="gguf-read-button" @onclick="OnRead">Read header</button>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="field field--wide" aria-live="polite">
            @if (Error is not null)
            {
                <div class="callout callout--failed" role="alert" data-testid="gguf-error">
                    <Icon Name="state-failed" /><div class="callout-body">@Error</div>
                </div>
            }
            @if (Summary is { } s)
            {
                <dl class="kv gguf-summary" data-testid="gguf-summary">
                    <dt>File</dt><dd class="num" data-testid="gguf-summary-file">@s.File@(s.SplitCount > 1 ? $" (+{s.SplitCount - 1} parts)" : "")</dd>
                    <dt>Architecture</dt><dd data-testid="gguf-summary-arch">@s.Architecture</dd>
                    <dt>Type</dt><dd>@(s.FileType ?? UiFormat.Missing)</dd>
                    <dt>Size</dt><dd>@UiFormat.Bytes(s.FileBytes)</dd>
                    <dt>Layers</dt><dd data-testid="gguf-summary-layers">@s.BlockCount.ToString(CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)</dd>
                    <dt>Trained context</dt><dd data-testid="gguf-summary-context">@(s.ContextLength is { } ctx ? ctx.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture) + " tokens" : UiFormat.Missing)</dd>
                    <dt>Pooling</dt><dd data-testid="gguf-summary-pooling">@(s.PoolingType ?? "none (chat model)")</dd>
                    <dt>Attention</dt><dd>@(s.CausalAttention == false ? "non-causal" : "causal")</dd>
                    <dt>Chat template</dt><dd>@(s.HasChatTemplate ? "in the file" : "none in the file")</dd>
                </dl>
                @if (Estimate is { } estimate)
                {
                    <div class="gguf-fit" data-testid="gguf-fit">
                        @FitLines(estimate.BudgetGiB, atLeast: false)
                    </div>
                }
            }
        </div>
    }
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The repo's GGUF variants (download shape); null for the folder shape.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<GgufVariant>? Variants { get; set; }

    /// <summary>True when the model's node runs llama.cpp on the CPU: the fit before a download counts no CUDA context.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool CpuOnly { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The repo's vision projectors (<c>mmproj-*</c>), listed apart from the variants.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<RepoFile> Projectors { get; set; } = [];

    [Parameter]
    public string SelectedVariant { get; set; } = "";

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> SelectedVariantChanged { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string SelectedProjector { get; set; } = "";

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> SelectedProjectorChanged { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The room on each GPU of the chosen node (one entry on a unified node); empty when unknown.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<GgufGpuRoom> Rooms { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>The folder on the node (folder shape); null for the download shape.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Folder { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The model GGUFs of a folder that holds several (from the agent's refusal); empty = type or leave blank.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<string> Candidates { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>The chosen file, relative to the folder.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string File { get; set; } = "";

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> FileChanged { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Reads the header of <see cref="File"/>.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnRead { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The header read.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public GgufSummary? Summary { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Why the header could not be read.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Error { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The live estimate of the current settings (for the fit lines).</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public GgufMemoryEstimate? Estimate { get; set; }

    private async Task OnFileChosenAsync(string? file)
    {
        File = file ?? "";
        await FileChanged.InvokeAsync(File);
        if (File.Length > 0)
        {
            await OnRead.InvokeAsync();
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// One line per GPU: "GPU 0: the GGUF estimate needs 8.9 GiB, 10.9 GiB free after the 2.5 GiB reserve", with its
    /// verdict. The need is named (<see cref="LlamaCppEditing.NeedText"/>, MN-239 item 2) because the placement's verdict
    /// on the same page measures the model's memory budget instead.
    /// </summary>
    private RenderFragment FitLines(double need, bool atLeast) =>
        @<ul class="plain-list gguf-fit-list">
            @if (Rooms.Count == 0)
            {
                <li class="muted">@LlamaCppEditing.NeedText(need, atLeast); choose the node to see its GPUs.</li>
            }
            @foreach (var room in Rooms)
            {
                bool? fits = LlamaCppEditing.Fits(need, room);
                <li class="budget-check @(fits == false ? "budget-check--over" : fits == true ? "budget-check--ok" : null)"
                    data-fits="@(fits switch { true => "true", false => "false", _ => "unknown" })">
                    <Icon Name="@(fits == true ? "check" : "warning")" />
                    <span>@LlamaCppEditing.FitText(need, room, atLeast)@(fits switch { true => " · fits", false => " · does not fit", _ => "" })</span>
                </li>
            }
        </ul>;

    private static string Slug(string value) =>
        new([.. value.ToLowerInvariant().Select(c => char.IsLetterOrDigit(c) ? c : '-')]);
}
